s10-p11 : Block
s10-p11 = prose (cons "The same treatment applies to user interfaces. A view is an interpretation of state; an edit is an operation relating the displayed representation and the underlying state. Bidirectional view laws express what round trips preserve and what information is lost. A view can be a diagram, a text editor, a table, a proof visualization, or an immersive spatial interface. Harel’s statecharts supply an established formal example of visual representations of stateful behavior ([66](#ref-66)). No one of these is privileged." nil)
